      {
        "id": 133742,
        "name": "jffdougan",
        "username": "jffdougan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-02T20:30:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Craig\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/48/2150_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Craig:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>MrLeRobot wrote:</b><br><blockquote><strong>Christopher wrote:</strong><br><blockquote>Glad to hear that you like both GTG and DHMG!\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nFor 2015, I took the resolution to not buy any more games, with the exception of SotM expansions and DHMG releases. I was utterly pleased when DHMG announced they've formed a partnership with you guys. My 2 favorites publishers working together is just plain awesome...! :)\n</blockquote></div>\nI'm in the same boat. Historically, I've had two auto-backs on Kickstarter. Greater Than Games and Dice Hate Me Games. When I was hired by Greater Than Games, that slashed my gaming expenses like crazy since now I just have access to GtG stuff.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Did you ever look at anything from the Evil Hat crew? If I had enough disposable income to regularly back Kickstarter projects, they'd be up there.</p>",
